architecture bonfyre-matrix
  canonical_name BonfyreMatrix
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Factorized participation
  layer institutional
  semantic_question How can one stable semantic subject lawfully acquire many addresses, presences, disclosures, and institutional relationships without becoming copied applications or a flattened tenant graph?
  purpose Native factorized substrate for evidence-bound semantic subjects, address constellations, recursively delegated institutions, and authenticated self-declared publication-presence projections across Life, Live, Shop, Work, and independent territories.
  maturity implemented
  owns MatrixSubject
  owns AddressConstellation
  owns CanonicalDomain
  owns StandingAddress
  owns PublicationPresence
  owns InstitutionDelegation
  consumes Authority
  consumes Evidence
  publishes AddressConstellation
  publishes PublicationPresence
  node_types MatrixSubject
  node_types AddressConstellation
  node_types StandingAddress
  node_types CanonicalDomain
  node_types AddressAlias
  node_types PublicationPresence
  node_types InstitutionDelegation
  edge_types addressed_as
  edge_types projects_as
  edge_types delegates_to
  internal_calculus global address uniqueness over subject identity; unbounded address multiplicity per subject
  internal_calculus host/path resolution selects an active exact presence over territory, world, audience, and requested representation
  internal_calculus controlled host resolution uses the longest registered DNS suffix; an explicit canonical host supplies a deliberate host alias rather than a copied institution
  internal_calculus StandingAddress membership is derived from active subject-presence factors and is never stored as a copied result array
  internal_calculus ordered disclosure membrane self -> household -> group -> community -> public -> market -> institution
  internal_calculus an authenticated actor may declare one local subject and its address constellation with a retained creation receipt; it never thereby receives delegated, financial, foreign, or institutional effect authority
  internal_calculus recursive delegation cycle rejection, after AuthorityGraph admits delegate over the parent institution
  internal_calculus RecursiveMatrixClosure compiles any exact resolved host/path Matrix cut into a virtual RO-Crate and Zarr v3 group: semantic identity/address/presence are resolved once; material, latent, execution, and economic planes stay sparse until their existing owners publish immutable evidence-bound references for that exact subject/presence cut
  invariant an address constellation locates one semantic subject; it does not copy that subject
  invariant a publication creates a presence projection while retaining its source presence and semantic identity
  invariant a web alias may redirect only to an address of the same semantic subject
  invariant a registered host supplies public context but never grants subject, institution, effect, or private-closure authority
  invariant a public URL aperture prepares only a reviewed Studio route on a configured host; it never observes, claims, fetches, or promotes a ForeignTwin
  invariant Matrix consults AuthorityGraph for institutional delegation; authenticated subject declaration records only a local Presence and does not grant authority itself
  invariant an authenticated actor may extend a local Matrix subject only when its stable subject identifier is rooted in that verified actor; another actor's or Aurekai-owned subject requires the separate AuthorityGraph path
  invariant institution kinds and subject kinds are extensible domain grammar, not a generic ERP ontology
  invariant a virtual Matrix crate is a compiled closure, not a new semantic object or package-owned record; re-materializing it preserves the canonical subject and address identity
  invariant a non-root closure address is a bounded local path on the controlled host and resolves through the same active Presence rule as HTML; it cannot name a foreign URL or substitute a host-wide closure for a subject cut
  invariant a Matrix crate structurally omits private/effect/economic/provider state not supplied by its owning closure; a RO-Crate or Zarr group is never treated as a complete viewer closure
  invariant a closure owner-reference is admitted only for an already-active exact Presence, names its independent owner, exact representation, digest and receipt, and cannot create a subject, Presence, disclosure, owner state, lifecycle, or authority
  forbidden_inference an address resolving -> read, effect, publication, or economic authority
  forbidden_inference a RO-Crate or Zarr closure -> a material body, latent comparability, model/provider route, Work permission, financial state, or effect authority
  forbidden_inference a receipted closure owner-reference -> a readable body, current owner state, viewer closure, provider availability, financial position, Work permission, or effect authority
  forbidden_inference a valid Studio session -> authority to add a Presence, StandingAddress, or alias to a subject it did not originate
  forbidden_inference a public or market presence -> a new canonical semantic object
  forbidden_inference a public URL prepared on the landing surface -> evidence, a ForeignTwin, canonical truth, or authority over the foreign system
  forbidden_inference a delegated institution -> transfer of private data closure or parent authority
  forbidden_inference accumulated presences -> a lawful disclosure regression
  forbidden_inference a StandingAddress member -> a canonical relationship or a completed Work result
  forbidden_inference a Fleming market median -> a comp, an appraisal, or a price for any single parcel
  forbidden_inference a taxpayer name on the roll -> the legal owner, a sole owner, or capacity to convey
  forbidden_inference a watched parcel -> an offer, an option, a lien position, or any claim on that parcel
  forbidden_inference a registered client entity -> an engagement, a contract, a billing account, or an entitlement
  forbidden_inference a budget cap on the financial membrane -> committed capital, an invoice, or funds on hand
  forbidden_inference a public profile view -> the absence of a private record; it is what the graph publishes, not all that exists
  forbidden_inference an agent holding an MCP write verb -> authority over a human submit line
  invariant a profile's self view is selected by the verified session alone; no path, query, or header can select it
  invariant a client registered through MCP and through HTTP resolves to one entity in one store
  invariant a foreign twin excluded by robots is receipted without its source URL being fetched
  invariant completing a WorkGraph node requires the lease token issued at claim; a valid-hex wrong token is refused by the queue as stale_claim
  forbidden_inference a claimed mission -> a completed one, or authority to complete it without the lease
  forbidden_inference an entity link -> consent by either party; it is a stated relationship, not an accepted one
  forbidden_inference a compiled Frappe schema -> an executed controller, hook, or migration; extraction is metadata only
  invariant a presence is bound once; the core refuses a re-bind, and a move is not emulated by delete and reinsert
  invariant a standing address stands only on an already-bound address
  invariant a web alias may bind only between two addresses of the same semantic subject
  invariant a workgraph failure carries a class from the scheduler's closed set, which decides retryability
  invariant a protocol projection is a carrier grammar over one semantic Matrix; it never becomes a second owner of the data
  invariant a capability quoted to an agent carries the same price the financial membrane reports; there is no second price list
  invariant an unverified payment is never treated as settled; with no facilitator the resource answers 402 and says why
  invariant a cross-carrier capability exchange uses one native ProtocolMachine identity; quote and payment presentation may be retained, while payment verification and execution remain impossible without an exercised rail-specific adapter
  invariant a protocol field the source does not carry is emitted null with a stated reason, never fabricated
  forbidden_inference a RESO or MISMO projection -> an MLS listing, a listing agreement, an appraisal, or a loan file
  forbidden_inference an OGC feature with null geometry -> an absent parcel; the roll carries area and length, not coordinates
  forbidden_inference an advertised A2A skill -> an agreement to perform it for any particular requester
  forbidden_inference an empty CAP, EPCIS, or OpenRTB collection -> absence in the world; nothing has been admitted to observe
  invariant a content type describes its own fields; an editor generates its form from that description and holds no second copy of any schema
  invariant the notes index lists only pages that are published AND guest-readable, so it can never advertise a page a reader cannot open
  forbidden_inference a published CMS page -> a disclosure decision; publishing and guest-readability are separate flags
  invariant an asset or theme is a ForeignTwin: admitted through the same observe right, robots preflight, receipt and content digest as any other foreign observation
  invariant a retained asset body is served only while it still hashes to its receipt; a digest mismatch is refused, not served
  invariant binding an asset to an account is an edge in the identity graph, which is what makes a shared cache of external things one account's expression
  forbidden_inference admitting an asset -> a licence, or any right in the underlying work
  forbidden_inference a bound theme -> ownership; it is a stated preference of that account
  invariant a session is authenticated and separately authorized; being signed in is never authority to mutate
  invariant a room describes its subject and is never a second way into it; readability is decided once, by the rule the reader path uses, so no surface can serve a body another surface refuses
  invariant a queue of unpublished things discloses its count and never its rows to a viewer who cannot act on them; the count is a fact about the institution, the rows are content nobody has published
  forbidden_inference a page that states a restriction -> a page that enforces it; the note room printed readable-by signed-in-accounts-only above the body it was serving to anyone
  invariant an operational surface carries a no-index directive and is named in robots.txt, because a surface reachable by a person is reachable by a crawler that followed the same link
  invariant the machine web is materialized, not generated per caller: a sitemap, a feed and a metadata block are the same bytes for every consumer, so ten thousand machine reads cost what one costs
  invariant a sitemap is a publication claim and carries only what the reader path would serve to a stranger; an unpublished thing listed there is one more way to leak it
  invariant an advertised alternate representation exists at the address it advertises; a rel=alternate promising JSON that returns HTML is a false statement about the surface
  invariant a machine consumer is offered a validator and answered 304 when it already holds the bytes, and HEAD is a first-class verb because it is how freshness is checked without paying for a body
  forbidden_inference a verified crawler identity -> authority to read anything private; identity resolution is not authorization here any more than anywhere else, and a user agent is a clue rather than a credential
  invariant a carrier projection never becomes a second owner of facts; a preview card, a sitemap entry and a payment quote are all projections of one state and cannot disagree with it or each other
  invariant a subject stands at explicit per-representation addresses as well as under content negotiation, because many machine consumers follow links and never send an Accept header
  invariant a manifest names every representation of a subject so one fetch discovers the family, and digests the representation rather than asserting a version of the subject
  invariant absent geometry is published as null with the reason; the observed roll gives an address and synthesising a centroid would turn a missing fact into a plausible one
  invariant machine readership is measured from the access log rather than assumed; a declared user agent is counted as a claim about purpose and never treated as identity or as a basis for access
  forbidden_inference a change published -> a change propagated; a pull-only surface waits for a crawler's own schedule, and a withdrawn claim keeps being asserted by every copy that has not been told
  invariant a foreign source is read through the cheapest deterministic representation it already publishes; HTML extraction and model interpretation are the last two rungs of a ladder, never the first move
  invariant discovery decides what to read and never becomes a second way to read it; every body that matters is admitted by the organ that owns foreign observation, so a parser works from bytes that still hash to their receipt
  invariant a probe verifies the representation is present, not that the server answered 200; a rejection page served with a success code otherwise records an affordance the source does not have and routes every later read into a carrier that will never answer
  invariant a source that declares nothing machine-legible is recorded as expensive rather than treated as normal; the cost of reading it is a property of that source and belongs in its passport
  forbidden_inference a source passport -> a claim about the world; it records how an institution wishes to be consumed and what our own probes observed, never what its documents assert
  invariant a push delivery is a notification and never content; the payload says a topic moved, and the bytes retained are the ones the origin serves on a re-read under the admission law
  invariant a hub's verification is refused unless the topic it names is exactly the topic that callback subscribed to; without that check a stranger enrols this institution into a subject it never chose
  invariant a subscription created with a secret refuses an unsigned delivery, and compares the signature in constant time; an early return leaks the digest one byte at a time
  invariant a notification triggers at most one re-read per minute per subscription, so a flood of pings cannot turn a callback into an amplifier aimed at the publisher
  invariant work provoked by a request happens after the reply and off the request path; a single-threaded organ that fetches inline can deadlock against itself when the topic it reads is one it serves
  invariant a receipted body is parsed only while it still hashes to its receipt; bytes that have drifted are not the bytes that were observed and cannot support any claim derived from them
  invariant a parsed foreign item is a candidate carrying its own provenance, recorded as what a source declared at an observed time, never as what is true or current or will occur
  invariant a subscription lease is renewed inside its own window; a lapsed lease is silent rather than loud, and a topic that stops delivering is indistinguishable from a source with no news
  invariant a WebSub renewal retains the subscription callback/token identity; parallel rows would multiply foreign rereads and make one source appear as several independent observations
  invariant a verified WebSub delivery writes only a coalesced SourceDirty notification; a bounded worker performs the later ForeignTwin reread, so repeated notifications normally produce one observation attempt
  invariant a callback without the receipt that authorized its subscription cannot induce a foreign read; notification reachability is not observe authority
  forbidden_inference an advertised hub -> a hub that exists; declaring one this institution does not run leaves a subscriber waiting for deliveries that can never arrive, which is worse for them than knowing to poll
  invariant an address withdrawn from a source index is recorded as a withdrawal; a claim loses its support when its source stops listing it, and every copy never told keeps asserting it
  invariant a source index is read where the source says it lives, not at a conventional path; a site may answer the conventional address with an unrelated document and a success code
  invariant a refusal by the observation law is reported as the refusal it is, never as a generic failure; a source whose robots cannot be reached is declined correctly rather than unavailable accidentally
  invariant a challenge page is recorded as the source declining machine reading and is not circumvented; a source may advertise an affordance in one document and gate it in another, and that contradiction is a fact about the source
  forbidden_inference a two hundred status -> the representation requested; an interstitial, a rejection page and a login wall are all served with success codes
  invariant session scope follows the account tier at login; a free account reads, a paid tier may also write
  invariant a client-institution hostname is a private AuthorityGraph aperture: every request requires an active exact institution grant, with read for GET/HEAD and write/admin for a mutation, before any legacy upstream is contacted; generic subscription tier or Bonfyre write scope never substitutes for the client grant
  invariant a client grant is re-evaluated on each request, so revocation or expiry denies an otherwise valid session immediately; it is a transport admission aperture and does not replace the managed product's object-level authority
  invariant a mutation reaching the CMS through nginx is held to write scope, because an auth subrequest is always a GET and cannot see the original verb
  forbidden_inference an authenticated session -> permission to change another person's content
  forbidden_inference a controlled client hostname -> a public institution, a crawlable route, a machine carrier, or read authority over its legacy estate
  forbidden_inference a paid Bonfyre account or generic write scope -> JRSS, AI Loss, Upper90, Leads, or any other client-estate authority
  invariant a person-facing surface is a flow: each step renders the next and carries its subject forward, rather than a panel of controls that each fire one call
  invariant the operator surface states what is open for decision, computed from the stores that hold it, and gives each open thing the one act that closes it
  invariant a queue count is counted, never inferred from the size of the page showing it; a page that stops at its limit reports the limit and understates what is open
  invariant an empty queue names what would fill it, because an empty queue is a fact about the institution rather than a gap in the page
  forbidden_inference the operator desk -> a feature index; a control with nothing open behind it is not offered, and the unsorted panel keeps its own address
  invariant a content type listing is generated from the type itself, so every declared type lists and creates without a per-type branch
  forbidden_inference an assessed value or a city median -> an appraisal, a comparable sale, a listing price, or advice
  invariant a protocol reaches a person as a flow over real state, not as a JSON endpoint they must already know exists
  invariant the commerce grammars quote from one service book, so x402, MPP, UCP, ACP and Beckn cannot disagree about a price
  invariant the executable catalogue is a subset of the service book, not the same set: x402 settles only what an organ can produce, while the shopping grammars may carry inventory no organ delivers
  forbidden_inference a priced entry in the book -> an x402-sellable capability; pricing is a fact about the book and delivery is a fact about the organs
  invariant an agent surface reaches the institution's own organs -- registry, service book, estate, local generation, every carrier -- because a surface that shows only activity lets an agent watch the system without being able to use it
  invariant a local generation path refuses when its chain is incomplete and names the missing link, rather than returning to the remote provider that a routing constraint sent the work away from
  invariant local generation is a resident service on loopback, not a per-call process launch; a five-gigabyte model reloaded for every prompt is a path nothing will actually route to
  invariant an internal organ that authenticates nobody is bound to loopback and denied every other address, because reachability is the whole of its security
  forbidden_inference a wrapper organ that names a backend -> a working path through it; bonfyre-moe passes a llama.cpp flag that llama.cpp renamed, and two projects moving separately skew whether or not either is broken
  invariant a failure that will recur identically is blocked rather than retried; an exhausted account rescheduled on a timer produces a stream of calls that cannot succeed and buries the errors that could
  forbidden_inference a large model file on disk -> a generation weight; a speech voice is neither, and counting it as one reports a runnable local path that cannot answer a prompt
  invariant an organ that writes state is told which store to write, never left to infer one from a home directory a service does not have
  invariant a durable row state that means work is in flight is reconciled against live runs; without reconciliation a process that dies without raising strands the row forever and the store reports activity that no actor is performing
  invariant a store with more than one writer is reclaimed by staleness, never by a startup sweep; a sweep that assumes single-instance hands the same work to two runners at once
  invariant a pause is scoped to what it can actually stop; a stop file that halts one daemon while other writers share its store leaves both readings true and neither complete
  forbidden_inference paused -> nothing is running; the flag describes the actor that owns it, not every actor writing to its database
  invariant usage telemetry never invalidates the response it describes; a completed and billed generation discarded during token accounting is paid for twice and delivered never
  invariant an empty protocol world names what it is waiting for and the one act that fills it, rather than presenting itself as complete
  forbidden_inference an empty CAP, EPCIS, WoT or OpenRTB world -> absence in reality; it is absence of an admitted source
  invariant a subject is addressable and answers with itself plus the operations that pertain to it, rather than a person navigating to a feature and filling a form
  invariant an aperture is computed per viewer from identity, the capability registry, runtime reachability, session closure, authority and cost; it is never a static menu
  invariant visual weight in an aperture is a projection of closure, so the strongest action is the one that viewer can most usefully take
  forbidden_inference an offered action -> permission already granted; the act still checks scope at the effect boundary
  forbidden_inference an absent action -> a missing feature; it is a closure for that viewer
  invariant a relation is a direction, offered only when the graph has somewhere to go; a direction the source cannot support is named rather than hidden
  invariant a lens alters selection and representation independently, so a selection can be shown differently and a representation can be reused over other objects
  invariant a lens lives in its address, not in a stored preference, so sharing the address shares the exact cut
  forbidden_inference a lens -> the default view; no cut is privileged over another
  invariant a room is navigation continuity with representational discontinuity: arrival is uniform, and what is found is shaped by what the subject is
  invariant a room states which of its bands the source cannot supply, rather than rendering an empty frame as though the data were merely missing
  invariant every carrier listed on a subject is a coordinate of that one subject, never a copy that could diverge from it
  invariant creation is read into a typed proposal and shown before anything exists; the person chooses the type, and a wrong reading costs a click
  forbidden_inference a composed reading -> the object already created; nothing exists until a type is chosen
  forbidden_inference publishing -> the purpose of creation; it is one projection of it
  invariant a composed type is created through the organ that owns that kind, so it is the same object every other surface sees
  invariant a sentence that proposes several things at once is read as a combination, offered above its parts, and creates each part through its own organ in order
  invariant a combination reports part by part: a part that failed is named as failed rather than omitted, because what was asked for and what became real are different facts
  forbidden_inference a combination -> a transaction; an earlier part survives a later part's refusal and is not rolled back
  invariant a room exists for a kind only when it was built for that kind; an unbuilt kind is named as unbuilt rather than served a generic frame
  invariant traversal is one gesture over changing object grammars: the movement stays fixed while each kind is drawn in its own terms
  invariant a traversal position lives in the address, so the same position is the same object for everyone and the sequence is shareable
  forbidden_inference a traversal sequence -> a ranking or a recommendation; nothing about the viewer selects or orders what appears
  invariant an interaction trace records the shape of an interaction -- subject kind, closure, offered actions -- never which subject a viewer looked at
  invariant a viewer is counted through a salted digest, so repetition is distinguishable from reload without retaining who they were
  invariant a shape is proven only when it both repeats and is seen by distinct viewers; anonymous traffic cannot prove a shape because its viewers cannot be told apart
  forbidden_inference a SurfaceCandidate -> a decision to build it; cooling a shape into a fixed page is a deliberate act the frontier never performs
  forbidden_inference an interaction trace -> a record of what any person did; it is the shape of an interaction, not its subject
  invariant a set of near-identical objects is compressed as a set, ordered so that like sits beside like; compressing each object alone leaves the shared structure unmeasured and unclaimed
  invariant the ordering is the lever, not the window size: a set laid out tree-by-tree hides its duplicates beyond any practical long-range window, while the same set laid out by relative path exposes them to a small one
  invariant a compression window is part of the frame, so the same window must be declared on the way out; an archive written with one and read without it is not corrupt, it is unreadable by a reader that never opted in
  invariant an archive replaces its original only after the original has been extracted again and compared entry for entry, symlinks and empty directories included
  forbidden_inference a listing of regular files -> the tree; a symlink and an empty directory are structure, and an archive built from a file list alone silently drops both
  invariant a response body that is not text/html is compressed too; nginx compresses only HTML unless told the other types, and every asset a page loads is paid for on every load
  native_format graf
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_matrix.h
  source_path engine/core/src/matrix.c
  source_path engine/core/include/bf_matrix_closure.h
  source_path engine/core/src/matrix_closure.c
  witness engine/core/tests/matrix_closure_test.c rejects a contribution whose Presence is not active for its subject, then emits an exact ObjectFabric reference without resolving any other owner plane
source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
source_path integrations/mcp/matrix_tools.json
source_path integrations/mcp/matrix_aperture.mjs
witness integrations/mcp/tests/matrix_aperture.test.mjs covers read-only native Matrix tool arguments, sparse closure claims and authenticated MCP transport; the rich mesh and recursive Python overlay remain active until their other tools and deployment paths reach parity
  source_path site/matrix/index.html
  source_path site/matrix/vgpu/htmx.ts
  source_path site/matrix/vgpu/matrix-vgpu.ts
  source_path site/matrix/surfaces/studio.html
  source_path packs/fleming-equity-group/evidence/estate.parquet/observation.parquet
  source_path components/BonfyreProject/src/main.c
  source_path deploy/nginx/aurekai-surfaces.conf
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-web-address.service
  source_path deploy/systemd/bonfyre-surface-fabric.service
  witness engine/core/tests/matrix_test.c
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_address_test.sh
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_address_test.sh compiles one native root resolution into both RO-Crate JSON-LD and a virtual Zarr v3 group, asserting exact Matrix identity and explicit unresolved owner planes
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_address_test.sh attaches an ObjectFabric reference to one exact root Presence and verifies identical RO-Crate/Zarr owner-reference projection through HTTP
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_address_test.sh resolves one plant path into distinct HTML, RO-Crate and Zarr coordinates with the same active Presence and rejects a foreign URL supplied as a closure path
  source_lineage Generation-10 factorized institutional matrix and address-constellation recovery, 2026-08-28
  interacts matrix-addresses-through-address-plane
  interacts matrix-standing-address-projects-to-surface
  interacts matrix-publication-requires-authority
  interacts matrix-presence-projects-to-surface
  interacts matrix-realizes-institutional-root
  interacts matrix-closure-references-artifact
  interacts matrix-closure-references-latent
  interacts matrix-closure-references-execution
  interacts matrix-closure-references-economic

interaction matrix-addresses-through-address-plane
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination address-plane
  relation resolved_location_candidate
  preserves one semantic subject across multiple lawful addresses while AddressPlane determines only route eligibility
  drops any implication that an address is readable, actionable, or semantically equivalent to another address
  forbidden_inference an AddressPlane route match -> authority over the Matrix subject
  binding engine/core/src/matrix.c

interaction matrix-standing-address-projects-to-surface
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination surface-ir
  relation live_query_membership_projection
  preserves a stable saved address and factorized active-presence membership while allowing HTML, API, MCP, A2A, CMS, Habitat, and filesystem carriers to project it
  drops any result-array ownership, effect permission, and claim that membership itself is canonical semantic state
  forbidden_inference a standing query result -> authority to mutate a matched subject
  witness engine/core/tests/matrix_test.c
  binding engine/core/src/matrix.c


interaction matrix-publication-requires-authority
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination authority-graph
  relation delegated_authority_admitted_projection
  preserves AuthorityGraph as the sole owner of delegation and institutional publication admission; an authenticated self-declaration is deliberately narrower and cannot assert a delegated role or effect right
  drops the authority grant implementation and its mutable edge store from Matrix
  forbidden_inference a Matrix presence -> a publish grant
  binding engine/core/src/matrix.c
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c

interaction matrix-presence-projects-to-surface
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination surface-ir
  relation presence_surface_input
  preserves subject identity, territory, disclosure scope, representation request, and source evidence for a surface projection
  drops any claim that a SurfaceIR rendering changes canonical subject or publication authority
  forbidden_inference a rendered surface -> a new subject or a completed publication effect
  binding cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  binding site/matrix/index.html
  binding site/matrix/vgpu/matrix-vgpu.ts
  binding site/matrix/surfaces/studio.html
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/auth_surface_test.sh

interaction matrix-realizes-institutional-root
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination institutional-root
  relation factorized_subject_and_owner_topology
  preserves the distinction between a Matrix subject/presence and the product or delegated estate that owns its local relationship closure
  drops any claim that all Matrix subjects belong to one tenant, product, or company
  forbidden_inference an institution hosting a Matrix presence -> ownership of every subject address or private data closure
  binding engine/core/src/matrix.c

interaction matrix-closure-references-artifact
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination artifact-graph
  relation presence_bound_owner_reference
  preserves the exact Matrix subject and active Presence, independent Artifact/Format ownership, representation identifier, immutable digest, and evidence receipt
  drops every artifact body, format conversion, readable-body decision, lifecycle, and publishing decision from Matrix
  forbidden_inference a material-plane closure reference -> a readable body, valid conversion, current artifact, license, or publication authority
  invalidates_on the exact Presence is withdrawn or a later owner receipt changes the artifact reference frontier
  witness engine/core/tests/matrix_closure_test.c
  binding engine/core/include/bf_matrix.h
  binding engine/core/src/matrix.c
  binding engine/core/src/matrix_closure.c

interaction matrix-closure-references-latent
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination latent-coordinate-fabric
  relation passported_projection_reference
  preserves subject/presence identity, declared latent representation, exact projection digest, and evidence receipt
  drops latent coordinates, encoder, source closure, comparability contract, learned inference, and any ranking decision from Matrix
  forbidden_inference a latent-plane closure reference -> comparable embedding, similarity, identity, model decision, or canonical fact
  invalidates_on the exact Presence is withdrawn or the named LatentCoordinateFabric owner emits a changed passported reference
  binding engine/core/include/bf_matrix.h
  binding engine/core/src/matrix_closure.c

interaction matrix-closure-references-execution
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination work-graph
  relation execution_owner_reference
  preserves only an evidence-bound reference from one active subject Presence to an independently-owned execution representation
  drops Work identity/state, target obligation, provider route, resource admission, authority, effect transition, and receipt interpretation from Matrix
  forbidden_inference an execution-plane closure reference -> queued Work, runnable capability, provider availability, a claimed mission, or effect authority
  invalidates_on the exact Presence is withdrawn or the independent execution owner changes its reference frontier
  binding engine/core/include/bf_matrix.h
  binding engine/core/src/matrix_closure.c

interaction matrix-closure-references-economic
  source bonfyre-matrix
  destination financial-metabolism
  relation economic_owner_reference
  preserves subject/presence identity, independently-owned economic representation, digest, and receipt identity only
  drops usage state, cost, allocation, agreement, funding, MoneyGraph facts, ledger position, settlement, and all spend/effect authority from Matrix
  forbidden_inference an economic-plane closure reference -> financial state, current balance, price, commitment, invoice, payment, settlement, or spend authority
  invalidates_on the exact Presence is withdrawn or the independent financial owner changes its evidence-bound reference frontier
  binding engine/core/include/bf_matrix.h
  binding engine/core/src/matrix_closure.c

architecture machine-membrane
  canonical_name MachineMembrane
  family institutional
  domain Institution / Machine-readable exchange
  layer institutional
  semantic_question How can one canonical state be delivered to thousands of machine consumers, and the machine-readable world be read back, without any carrier becoming a second owner of a fact or any cost scaling with the number of readers?
  purpose Two-way boundary to the machine internet: materialized outbound projections across discovery files, embedded metadata, per-subject artifact families, change streams and eighteen carrier grammars; inbound discovery of how each foreign source publishes, read through the cheapest deterministic representation it already offers and admitted under the foreign observation law.
  summary The two-way boundary between this institution and the machine-readable
    internet. Outbound it materializes one canonical state into discovery files,
    embedded metadata, per-subject artifact families, change streams and eighteen
    carrier grammars. Inbound it discovers how a foreign source publishes, reads it
    through the cheapest deterministic representation that source already offers,
    and admits every body through the foreign observation law. Neither direction
    owns a fact: both are projections of, or observations into, state owned
    elsewhere.
  maturity implemented
  native_format graf
